      "receiptId": "cabbage-sauce.html-1",
      "receiptSource": "Original Receipt in \u0027\u003Ci\u003EThe Art of Cookery, Made Plain and Easy\u003C/i\u003E\u0027 by Hannah Glasse, 1747 (\u003Ca href=\u0022references.html#glasse-1747\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003EGlasse 1747\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E);",
      "receiptText": "\u003Cb\u003ETO dress a goose with onions or cabbage.\u003C/b\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\nSALT the goose for a week, then boil it. It will take an hour. You may either make onion-sauce as we do for ducks, or cabbage boiled, chopped, and stewed in butter, with a little pepper and salt; lay the goose in the dish, and pour the sauce over it. It eats very good with either.\u003Cbr\u003E"
